  "title": "IMEXP routes numeric real inputs in [-300, 300] through Excel's worksheet EXP and uses CRT exp/cos/sin elsewhere",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 build 20527, IMEXP(inumber) evaluates numeric real inputs in [-300, 300] via Excel's worksheet EXP kernel before complex text formatting, whereas complex text inputs or magnitudes outside [-300, 300] evaluate CRT exp(re) * (cos(im) + sin(im) i). Empty text \"\" returns #NUM! while a blank cell returns \"1\". All 1,049 full-bank IMEXP rows match.",
